⭐ SDOA WHITEPAPER — VERSION 5.3 (Unified Architecture & Aesthetic Standard)Date: 2026‑06‑19Classification: Canonical — Architecture, Governance, & Design DoctrineSECTION 1 — EXECUTIVE SUMMARYSelf‑Describing Object Architecture (SDOA) is a polyglot, sovereign, manifest‑driven architecture in which every module declares its own identity, dependencies, capabilities, documentation, lifecycle, and aesthetic parameters directly inside its own file.  SDOA eliminates structural and presentation chaos by making code modularity and visual styling two sides of the same sovereign coin. Volume 5.3 formally binds technical engineering rules with "The Aesthetic Standard," creating an uncompromised, self-documenting technical environment.  SECTION 2 — CORE ARCHITECTURAL & THEMATIC AXIOMS2.1 The Sovereignty PrincipleEvery module is a sovereign. A sovereign completely owns its source files, its manifest, its local variant tree, its isolated data catalogs, and its matching localized stylesheets (*.prim.css or *.feature.css).  Forbidden: No sovereign may reach into another module's directory or mutate another module’s state.  Visual Scope: Global design tokens are locked into a single source of truth (ui/tokens.css). Components consume these tokens but dictate their layout execution locally.  2.2 Three-Layer Structural & Visual MappingEvery operation and visual asset flows through exactly three rigid vertical layers. No layer skipping is permitted.  LayerSystem Assignment   TXT+ 4Visual Presentation RoleLayer 1Features (*.feature.js)Composition & Intent: Loads layout templates (*.schema.json) and arranges primitives inside layout containers. Never hardcodes HTML elements or touches raw CSS styles directly.  Layer 2Primitives (*.prim.js)Reusable Visual Atoms: Renders raw pixels and directly executes co-located *.prim.css files. Has zero knowledge of application domain rules or back-end schemas.  Layer 3Adapters / Services / WorkflowsInfrastructure Data: Handles IPC routing, backend operations, and state changes via StateStore. Completely decoupled from visual presentation.  SECTION 3 — THE AESTHETIC STANDARD (VISUAL DESIGN TOKENS)The visual layout represents an "Industrial Minimalist meets Sacred Geometry" framework. The default presentation properties inside ui/tokens.css are legally enforced by the Migration & Compliance Pipeline (MCP).  3.1 Chromatic Tokens (The Volcanic Ash Palette)--color-canvas-bg: #1A1410 — Monolithic, heavy background base echoing warm volcanic slag.--color-core-amber: #F0C674 — High-luminance accent reserved for system singularties and functional points.--color-filament-gold: #E8B85C — Primary structural vector line strokes and prime typography.--color-filament-brass: #D1A45A — Secondary containment strokes and layout wireframing grids.--color-bronze-muted: #9A8050 — Low-hierarchy, machine-readable monospaced telemetry data.--color-sink-crimson: #2A1215 — Stable, desaturated dark crimson console backdrop for system failure alerts.--color-sink-coral: #FF8A80 — Pure industrial alert coral text for stack tracing.3.2 Typographic TensionsThe Monumental Title Axis: Headings and core identity fields are bound to classical Georgia, serif formats using a wide, tracking-heavy letter-spacing: 14px; rule to convey monumental structural weight.The Utilitarian Code Axis: Subtitles, parameters, and metadata values snap to flat, industrial monospace typography with a rigid letter-spacing: 6px; format, preserving machine-readable precision.SECTION 4 — MANIFEST & METADATA CONTRACTS (v5.3 SCHEMAS)Every module must carry a top-level manifest file contract. Manifests bind technical requirements to style profiles.  JavaScript// ------------------------------------------------------------------
