SECTION 5 — AUTOMATED EVOLUTION & VISUAL ANTI-ENTROPYThe Innovation Detector operates alongside the Reuse Mapper within the MCP to guarantee that neither code structures nor visual styling experience drift or entropy over time.  5.1 UI Primitive & Schema DetectionAST Structural Clustering: The pipeline continuously reviews front-end JSX/DOM fragment layouts. If nearly identical layout structures appear across 3 or more places inline, the Innovation Detector flags them, extracting them into a brand-new, standalone generic Layer 2 Primitive.  Inline Form Externalization: If multiple features implement duplicate data-entry surfaces inline, the system extracts the structural description out of the JavaScript view layers and generates a centralized schema file under ui/data/schemas/.  5.2 The Token Detector GateThe Token Detector acts as the visual system's immunologist.  Heuristic: It reviews all local styles, grouping raw values by color channels, padding sizes, and border treatments.  Action: If the exact same un-tokenized color or spacing parameter is repeated in 3 or more components, the Token Detector auto-generates a proposal to strip the local override and declare it as an official shared variable inside ui/tokens.css. This enforces the baseline visual standard programmatically.  SECTION 6 — FEDERATED INNOVATION SYNC PROTOCOL (FISP)When the Innovation Detector uncovers a generic rule, unique workflow pattern, or newly tokenized component layout, the system opens an optional, secure gateway to share the breakthrough with the public library ecosystem via FISP v1.1.6.1 The Unified Innovation EnvelopeJSON{
